            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0628" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.01/299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-18T19:00:00+09:00">November 18, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 18—11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>550. Our 540, November 13, 11 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>It is reported in the papers today that the Foreign Minister presented to
                        the Cabinet for approval an instrument providing for the recognition on
                        November 25 of the Franco regime.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Foreign Office informally advises us that any report indicating that a
                        decision has been reached is premature. The Foreign Office confirms that
                        recognition of Franco regime is “under consideration” but it adds that the
                        final decision might be in the negative. However, as an indication of the
                        probable nature of such final decision the Foreign Office invited attention
                        to the influence on the general international situation of the
                        Anti-Communist Pact. We take this to mean that the decision will be in the
                        affirmative.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>It is also reported in the press that a plan is under consideration
                        whereby Germany and Italy would recognize “Manchukuo”.<anchor n="21"
                            xml:id="d632-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
